# Shell scripts must use LF. core.autocrlf=true is set at the system level on
# Windows, which rewrites these to CRLF on checkout; bash (Git Bash/WSL) then
# fails to parse them (e.g. `syntax error near unexpected token '('`). Forcing
# eol=lf keeps deploy scripts runnable regardless of the host autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
